{{!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  training/sections.hbs — every training section, discovered from content.

  A SECTION IS A POST: tagged #training-section, primary tag = the section tag,
  and its slug == that tag's slug (so it lands at /training/{slug}/ — see
  routes.yaml). The post BODY is the section overview.

  This used to be a hand-written list of five {{> section-item}} calls kept in
  sync with a route-per-section block in routes.yaml. Both are gone: sections
  are queried, and ORDER is published_at asc — backdate a section post to move
  it earlier. Adding a section is now Ghost-Admin-only.

  Params (passed straight through to training/section-item):
    view  — "card" (the /training/ roadmap) | "nav" (rail) | "search"
            | "jsonld" | "jsonld-ref"
    cur   — slug of the section being viewed (nav active state)
    curId — id of the lesson being viewed (nav active state)

  limit="50": Ghost rejects limit="all" in {{#get}}, and 50 sections is far
  past any realistic path length. `@number`/`@first` supply the step number and
  the jsonld-ref comma suppression that used to be hand-written params.
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
{{#get "posts" filter="tag:hash-training-section" order="published_at asc" limit="50" include="tags"}}
  {{#foreach posts}}
    {{!-- Params live on THIS partial's context (two frames up: past #foreach and
         past #get), so they're reached with ../../ — a single ../ lands on the
         #get result scope, which has no view/cur/curId and silently blanks every
         section-item. --}}
    {{> "training/section-item" view=../../view cur=../../cur curId=../../curId n=@number first=@first}}
  {{/foreach}}
{{/get}}
